        "heading_wPhVgD": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "sub_heading": "Tapes For Construction/Municipal",
            "heading": "Most Common Adhesive Tapes Used In The Construction Industry",
            "highlight_style": "none",
            "highlight_font_style": "italic",
            "highlight_style_color": "",
            "highlight_text_color": "",
            "heading_size": "h3",
            "rich_text_cstm": "<p> </p>"
          }
        },
        "collapsible_item_w8RiKT": {
          "type": "collapsible_item",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "heading": "Acrylic Adhesive Tapes",
            "content": "<p>Acrylic tapes provide a long-term durable solution that makes them ideally suited for the construction industry. Some of their key properties include performing well in extreme temperatures, becoming stronger over time, and being used to create an airtight seal in a home. They also have the advantage of producing no off-gassing as well as not polluting landfills.</p>",
            "custom_liquid": "",
            "page": "",
            "open": true,
            "use_subtext_color": false
          }
        },
        "collapsible_item_tVVp8w": {
          "type": "collapsible_item",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "heading": "Masking Tape",
            "content": "<p>Masking tape is frequently used to protect surfaces such as walls and floors when painting; however, it can also be used in conjunction with other construction site activities such as sanding. Masking tapes remove cleaning and improve efficiency by protecting surfaces from paint or damage well, which usually eliminates the need for rework. They can be used in indoor and outdoor applications and are quick and simple to install.</p>",
            "custom_liquid": "",
            "page": "",
            "open": false,
            "use_subtext_color": false
          }
        },
        "collapsible_item_c4a4p8": {
          "type": "collapsible_item",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "heading": "Duct Tape",
            "content": "<p>Duct tape is a highly durable and waterproof tape comprised of a cloth backing layer that has been coated in polyethylene. The construction industry often uses duct tape for strapping or bundling materials at a job site. It is also used for making both temporary and permanent repairs and is available in a variety of colors to suit different surfaces and applications.</p>",
            "custom_liquid": "",
            "page": "",
            "open": false,
            "use_subtext_color": false
          }
        },
        "collapsible_item_JgUQL4": {
          "type": "collapsible_item",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "heading": "Safety Barricade Tape",
            "content": "<p>In certain instances, non-adhesive tapes are required, such as for warning workers of a hazardous area. Barricade tapes are used for this purpose. They have messages written on them with high voltage warnings, wet paint warnings, and more, and are strung up around the dangerous area. Floor marking tapes are another similar type of safety tape that can be used to make workers aware of dangerous areas.</p>",
            "custom_liquid": "",
            "page": "",
            "open": false,
            "use_subtext_color": false
          }
        },
        "collapsible_item_et7KBw": {
          "type": "collapsible_item",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "heading": "Foil Tapes",
            "content": "<p><a href=\"/pages/foil-tape\" title=\"Foil Tape\">Foil tapes</a> are made with a metal-foil backing which has been specially engineered to be malleable and conductive. The types of tapes are often quite durable and come in several varieties to meet the needs of differing applications. Aluminum foil tape is one type, which is the most commonly used throughout the construction industry. These types of tapes are used for purposes such as light or heat reflection, HVAC systems, and splice detection.</p>",
            "custom_liquid": "",
            "page": "",
            "open": false,
            "use_subtext_color": false
          }
        },
        "collapsible_item_RRV3AF": {
          "type": "collapsible_item",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "heading": "Double-Sided Tape",
            "content": "<p>Double-sided tape has adhesive on both sides and is designed to bond two surfaces together by adhering to them both, which spreads the stress load. Double-sided tapes can be used to bond a wide variety of materials such as glass, wood, steel, concrete, foam, and plastic. It can be used to attach insulation to walls, hold down protective carpeting during the construction process, overlap house wrap seams, and more.</p>",
            "custom_liquid": "",
            "page": "",
            "open": false,
            "use_subtext_color": false
          }
        },
        "collapsible_item_kw9UHA": {
          "type": "collapsible_item",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "heading": "Electrical Tapes",
            "content": "<p>Electrical tapes are usually made from a type of vinyl due to its durability and are used to insulate electrical splices or bundle wire and cable. Black electrical tapes are commonly used within the construction industry, however colorful electrical tapes also exist and are used in phasing tasks where it’s essential to have wire voltage strength or function labeled.</p>",
            "custom_liquid": "",
            "page": "",
            "open": false,
            "use_subtext_color": false
          }
        }
      },
